<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Quadratic equation from theatre seating (non-monic)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>
Rows of seats are arranged in a theatre. There are \((2x - {@b@})\) rows, and each row contains \(x\) seats. Altogether, {@T@} seats are arranged.
</p>

<p>(a) Form a quadratic equation, in standard form, representing the situation.</p>
<p>[[input:eqn1]] [[validation:eqn1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>(b) Determine the value of \(x\).</p>
<p>\(x =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>

<p>
Let \(x\) be the number of seats in each row.
</p>

<p>
The number of rows is \(2x - {@b@}\), and each row has \(x\) seats. Multiplying the number of rows by the number of seats per row gives the total number of seats:
</p>

<p>
\[
x(2x - {@b@}) = {@T@}
\]
</p>

<p>
Step 1: Expand the left-hand side.
</p>

<p>
\[
2x^2 - {@b@}x = {@T@}
\]
</p>

<p>
Step 2: Rearrange into standard quadratic form (equal to zero).
</p>

<p>
\[
2x^2 - {@b@}x - {@T@} = 0
\]
</p>

<p>
Step 3: Factorise. Because the coefficient of \(x^2\) is \(2\), the factors take the form \((x - r)(2x + s)\):
</p>

<p>
\[
{@qeq_factored@}
\]
</p>

<p>
Step 4: Apply the zero product rule and solve each factor.
</p>

<p>
\[
x = {@sol@} \quad \text{or} \quad x = {@negroot@}
\]
</p>

<p>
Since the number of seats in a row cannot be negative, we reject the negative solution. Therefore:
</p>

<p>
\[
x = {@sol@}
\]
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
